# tools/9run --dialog rules for 9front's installer (inst/start): its
# defaults (cwfs64x, GPT, 9fat, US_Eastern, ...) except where it has none.
# DEV is the target disk (sdE0 when installing the build VM's disk);
# callers substitute it. Older external Monolith tracing tools used
# sdE3 and prepended snapshot rules; this remains an installer fixture.
Task to do \[finish\]: *	finish
!now done halting	!done
Disk to partition .*\[no default\]: *	DEV
Install mbr or gpt .*\[no default\]: *	gpt
>>> *	w\nq
Plan 9 partition to subdivide .*: *	/dev/DEV/plan9
Cwfs cache partition .*: *	/dev/DEV/fscache
Cwfs worm partition .*: *	/dev/DEV/fsworm
Cwfs other partition .*: *	/dev/DEV/other
Plan 9 FAT partition .*\[no default\]: *	/dev/DEV/9fat
Initialize FAT on EFI system partition .*\[no default\]: *	yes
Distribution disk .*\[no default\]: *	/
\[no default\]: *	!fail
.*\[[^]]*\]:? *	''
